{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall be blessed above all the peoples.</b> More than all the peoples, in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 28:1): ״ונתנך ה' אלהיך עליון על כל גויי הארץ״ — and HaShem your Elohim will set you supreme above all the nations of the earth. For just as the Blesser mentioned in the verse ״וברכך״ — 'and He blessed you' — is greater than all elohim, so you, the blessed one of Him, shall be blessed above all the peoples. Or one may say 'above all the peoples' means from the mouth of all the peoples, for they shall all bless you and acknowledge your excellence."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:25.738776452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}